.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.hf_cache/

# submission_artifacts/ is GENERATED by run_demo.py and IS committed: the brief asks for
# run.log, evidence.json, evidence.md, manifests/, ledgers/, checkpoints/ and performance.json
# as submission links, so the graded copy ships with the repo.
#
# The one exception is the tokenized shards. They are 27 MB of regenerable binary, they are not
# in the structure the brief lists, and their integrity is already checkable from the committed
# manifest, which records every shard's content, index and identity hash. run_demo.py rebuilds
# them byte-identically as step 1.
submission_artifacts/shards/

# The repository root ignores *.log, which would silently swallow run.log - and run.log is one of
# the four links the assignment asks to be submitted. Re-include it explicitly.
!submission_artifacts/run.log
